// Nova is a third Bedrock embedding envelope: {taskType: SINGLE_EMBEDDING, singleEmbeddingParams: {...}}.
// Before support existed this was a 400 from DetermineEmbeddingModelType, which knew only Titan and
// Cohere. embeddingPurpose and text.truncationMode are required by AWS with no defaults, so a body
// missing either is a 400 - reaching 200 here proves both were supplied.

// dimensions -> embeddingDimension (256/384/1024/3072 only; anything else is an AWS enum 400, so a
// 1024-long vector proves the value was forwarded rather than dropped). task_type -> embeddingPurpose,
// whose enum is Nova's own: TEXT_RETRIEVAL is valid, the OpenAI-ish RETRIEVAL_DOCUMENT is not.

// The data URI prefix is stripped and the bytes go to singleEmbeddingParams.image.source.bytes, with
// format derived from the media type - AWS requires it, rejects 'jpg', and verifies the name against
// the bytes it detects, so a mis-derived format is a 400 rather than a wrong vector.

// detailLevel picks the resolution Nova reads an image at; DOCUMENT_IMAGE is the higher one, meant for
// text on a page, and pairs with embeddingPurpose DOCUMENT_RETRIEVAL. This row is the happy path;
// 114.A5 is the one that proves the key actually reaches AWS rather than being dropped.

// embeddingMode is required on video with no AWS default; Bifrost sends AUDIO_VIDEO_COMBINED unless the
// caller names one. SEPARATE is the only shape in the embeddings API where ONE input yields TWO
// vectors for different modalities, which is why each carries its own modality label.

// taskType SINGLE_EMBEDDING is what DetectInvokeRequestType routes on. It shares the taskType field
// with the Canvas image tasks, so a wrong branch here sends an embedding body down the image path;
// before support existed this body fell through to the chat schema and AWS answered "required key
// [messages] not found". The response must come back in Nova's envelope, not Titan's {embedding, ...}
// or Cohere's {embeddings, response_type}.

// The native body travels through the canonical schema and is rebuilt on the way out, so every field
// needs a home in both directions: format becomes a media type and is derived back, detailLevel and
// embeddingPurpose ride in ExtraParams. A dropped detailLevel would still return 200, so what this
// row pins is the format round trip - a lost format is a 400 from AWS, which requires it.
